					<description><![CDATA[Animals are unencumbered by moral conscious; nature is indeed red in tooth and claw. Their animal instincts are honed by thousands of years of adaptation. Although we are only talking monkeys, humans stand apart from the animal kingdom because of their evolved brains which allow us to create anthropomorphic projections upon animals.]]></description>
			<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Animals are unencumbered by moral conscious; nature is indeed red in tooth and claw. Their animal instincts are honed by thousands of years of adaptation. Although we are only talking monkeys, humans stand apart from the animal kingdom because of their evolved brains which allow us to create anthropomorphic projections upon animals.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
		
